# The Piper PA-28-180 Cherokee's livery: white, with dark red wingtips, fin and cheatline.
# src/gfx/parts.hpp says how a coat is read.
#
# Each box is in the model's body frame, metres from its origin: +x forward,
# +y starboard, +z down. Measured off the model's own sections
# (assets/models/pa28.mesh): a coat all over is the whole model's box; a
# wingtip's is beyond 88% of the wing's semispan; a fin's is above the
# fuselage's top at the tail, aft of the tail's leading edge; a cheatline's
# is along the fuselage's sides, between the heights given.
#
#    NAME          R   G   B       X0      X1       Y0      Y1      Z0     Z1
name White with dark red trim
coat tip-left    150  30  30    -2.40    3.73    -5.44   -4.70   -1.66   1.37
coat tip-right   150  30  30    -2.40    3.73     4.70    5.44   -1.66   1.37
coat fin         150  30  30    -3.80   -2.40    -0.60    0.60   -1.66  -0.20
coat cheatline   150  30  30    -3.80    3.73    -0.75    0.75   -0.20  -0.08
